97d6043c-b366-4446-a4f3-1dec6d15da42	╨С╨░╤А╨░╨╝╤Г╨╜╨┤╨╕ ╤Б ╨╝╨░╤А╨╛╨║╨║╨░╨╜╤Б╨║╨╕╨╝╨╕ ╤Б╨┐╨╡╤Ж╨╕╤П╨╝╨╕	lunch	457	25	14	57	{╨╝╨╛╤А╨╡╨┐╤А╨╛╨┤╤Г╨║╤В╤Л,╤А╤Л╨▒╨░}	[{"name": "╨С╨░╤А╨░╨╝╤Г╨╜╨┤╨╕", "grams": 100}, {"name": "╨Ь╨╛╨╗╨╛╤В╤Л╨╣ ╤В╨╝╨╕╨╜", "grams": 2.5}, {"name": "╨Ъ╨╕╨╜╨╖╨░", "grams": 52.5}, {"name": "╨Я╨░╨┐╤А╨╕╨║╨░", "grams": 0.5}, {"name": "╨Я╨╡╤А╨╡╤Ж ╤З╨╕╨╗╨╕", "grams": 0.5}, {"name": "╨з╨╡╤Б╨╜╨╛╨║", "grams": 100}, {"name": "╨Ы╨╕╨╝╨╛╨╜", "grams": 50}, {"name": "╨Ю╨╗╨╕╨▓╨║╨╛╨▓╨╛╨╡ ╨╝╨░╤Б╨╗╨╛", "grams": 75}]	https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/4o4wh11761848573.jpg	2026-05-03 20:15:15.396+00	2026-10-06 13:02:27.243+00	[]	step 1\r\nTip all the dressing ingredients into a food processor with a pinch of salt and blitz to a dressing. Slash the fish three times on each side, coat with half of the dressing, then set aside to marinate for about 30 mins.\r\n\r\nstep 2\r\nHeat oven to 220C/fan 200C/gas 7. Place the fish on a roasting tray, then cook in the oven for 20 mins until the flesh is firm and the eyes have turned white. Serve the fish with the rest of the dressing and steamed couscous or rice.\r\n\r\nstep 3\r\nKNOW HOW: HOW TO COOK IT: Cooking barramundi on the bone, as we have done here, has its advantages тАУ it will stay more moist during cooking, and some would say that the flavour is enhanced, too. If you want to take out the bones they are easy to locate and less likely to be lodged in the fillet if the fish is cooked whole. Fillets can be simply pan-fried or grilled. If you like trout, you will really enjoy the flavour of barramundi, which lends itself to similar ingredients and cooking methods тАУ citrus flavours are particularly good, as are garlic and wild mushrooms. Simply roasting the fish with some fresh herbs, olive oil and seasoning is delicious, and in the summer months you could barbecue it, too. One thing that you mustnтАЩt miss are the cheeks or тАШpearlsтАЩ of the fish, these are simply lovely, moist and really sweet тАУ well worth leaving the head on for!	1	\N	Australian	["╤Г╨╢╨╕╨╜"]	t	https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/barramundi-moroccan-spices	mealdb:53103	[{"id": "8e72aaa4-934f-40c8-aaf2-0afce5f7d149", "name": "╨С╨░╤А╨░╨╝╤Г╨╜╨┤╨╕", "unit": "╨│", "grams": 100, "amount": 100, "ingredientId": "0c9ff5cb-6933-4889-bc6e-3d93e52f03c0", "originalString": "100 ╨│"}, {"id": "17bf13ec-a954-4968-816d-9de0e6f5a9f1", "name": "╨Ь╨╛╨╗╨╛╤В╤Л╨╣ ╤В╨╝╨╕╨╜", "unit": "╨│", "grams": 2.5, "amount": 2.5, "ingredientId": "0858e27e-aeba-4065-8384-85c4d4fc62a5", "originalString": "2.5 ╨│"}, {"id": "90c2d322-f1ed-4ff7-86c1-4a8b1be2af65", "name": "╨Ъ╨╕╨╜╨╖╨░", "unit": "╨│", "grams": 52.5, "amount": 52.5, "ingredientId": "91b7fcb8-7a96-438b-8f70-bca57c96e463", "originalString": "52.5 ╨│"}, {"id": "9100e619-55b7-4654-95e1-ed0c665f5ad9", "name": "╨Я╨░╨┐╤А╨╕╨║╨░", "unit": "╨│", "grams": 0.5, "amount": 0.5, "ingredientId": "85045806-3a18-4d35-ad01-0230c0cb98d2", "originalString": "0.5 ╨│"}, {"id": "2a1465a0-8ec7-4a89-bc82-892f3cb6b50f", "name": "╨Я╨╡╤А╨╡╤Ж ╤З╨╕╨╗╨╕", "unit": "╨│", "grams": 0.5, "amount": 0.5, "ingredientId": "b976dce4-53c5-496d-bb37-a394d0de4e02", "originalString": "0.5 ╨│"}, {"id": "0ada2b7a-33a0-4b6e-9108-c681fb1b3c0a", "name": "╨з╨╡╤Б╨╜╨╛╨║", "unit": "╨│", "grams": 100, "amount": 100, "ingredientId": "91e7717c-e7a3-40d1-ad26-cbf9f854ab62", "originalString": "100 ╨│"}, {"id": "a9932f5d-bb85-416d-b627-7fec3d609c96", "name": "╨Ы╨╕╨╝╨╛╨╜", "unit": "╨│", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "2424a9f1-7d3e-4caf-afdf-ea30bcef37d0", "originalString": "50 ╨│"}, {"id": "04a73c5a-f77f-4b11-8424-2c3b3e27b3e2", "name": "╨Ю╨╗╨╕╨▓╨║╨╛╨▓╨╛╨╡ ╨╝╨░╤Б╨╗╨╛", "unit": "╨╝╨╗", "grams": 75, "amount": 75, "ingredientId": "bbc2d001-a24b-49ee-b8ec-16e74e7297ef", "originalString": "75 ╨╝╨╗"}]	["gluten-free", "lactose-free", "high-protein"]
6c135bf0-b4cc-465a-8367-440f5c6cfb18	╨Ф╨╛╨╝╨░╤И╨╜╨╕╨╡ ╨╝╨░╨╜╨┤╨░╨╖╨╕	lunch	576	32	18	72	{╨╗╨░╨║╤В╨╛╨╖╨░,╨│╨╗╤О╤В╨╡╨╜,╤П╨╣╤Ж╨░}	[{"name": "╨Ь╤Г╨║╨░ ╤Б ╤А╨░╨╖╤А╤Л╤Е╨╗╨╕╤В╨╡╨╗╨╡╨╝", "grams": 50}, {"name": "╨б╨░╤Е╨░╤А", "grams": 90}, {"name": "╨п╨╣╤Ж╨╛", "grams": 50}, {"name": "╨Ь╨╛╨╗╨╛╨║╨╛", "grams": 240}]	https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/thazgm1555350962.jpg	2026-05-03 20:15:57.415+00	2026-10-06 13:02:27.244+00	[]	This is one recipe a lot of people have requested and I have tried to make it as simple as possible and I hope it will work for you. Make sure you use the right flour which is basically one with raising agents. Adjust the amount of sugar to your taste and try using different flavours to have variety whenever you have them.\r\nYou can use Coconut milk instead of regular milk, you can also add desiccated coconut to the dry flour or other spices like powdered cloves or cinnamon.\r\nFor тАЬhealthy lookingтАЭ mandazis do not roll the dough too thin before frying and use the procedure I have indicated above.\r\n\r\n1. Mix the flour,cinnamon and sugar in a suitable bowl.\r\n2. In a separate bowl whisk the egg into the milk\r\n3. Make a well at the centre of the flour and add the milk and egg mixture and slowly mix to form a dough.\r\n4. Knead the dough for 3-4 minutes or until it stops sticking to the sides of the bowl and you have a smooth surface.\r\n5. Cover the dough with a damp cloth  and allow to rest for 15 minutes.\r\n6. Roll the dough on a lightly floured surface into a 1cm thick piece.\r\n7. Using a sharp small knife, cut the dough into the desired size setting aside ready for deep frying.\r\n8. Heat your oil in a suitable pot and gently dip the mandazi pieces to cook until light brown on the first side then turn to cook on the second side.\r\n9. Serve them warm or cold	1	\N	Kenyan	["╨╖╨░╨▓╤В╤А╨░╨║"]	t	http://chef-raphael.com/home-made-mandazi-recipe/#more-106	mealdb:52967	[{"id": "49a10792-a5e9-48d7-ae3c-74e9bd67907a", "name": "╨Ь╤Г╨║╨░ ╤Б ╤А