a0968f77-58a4-49b5-876e-70841200d762	╨Э╨╛╤А╨▓╨╡╨╢╤Б╨║╨╛╨╡ ╨║╨░╤А╤В╨╛╤Д╨╡╨╗╤М╨╜╨╛╨╡ ╨╗╨╡╤Д╤Б╨╡	lunch	1398	77	43	175	{╨╗╨░╨║╤В╨╛╨╖╨░,╨│╨╗╤О╤В╨╡╨╜}	[{"name": "╨Ъ╨░╤А╤В╨╛╤Д╨╡╨╗╤М", "grams": 150}, {"name": "╨б╨╛╨╗╤М", "grams": 5}, {"name": "╨б╨░╤Е╨░╤А", "grams": 5}, {"name": "╨а╨░╤Б╤В╨╛╨┐╨╗╨╡╨╜╨╜╨╛╨╡ ╨╝╨░╤Б╨╗╨╛", "grams": 60}, {"name": "╨Ц╨╕╤А╨╜╤Л╨╡ ╤Б╨╗╨╕╨▓╨║╨╕", "grams": 60}, {"name": "╨Ь╤Г╨║╨░ ╨╛╨▒╤Й╨╡╨│╨╛ ╨╜╨░╨╖╨╜╨░╤З╨╡╨╜╨╕╤П", "grams": 360}, {"name": "╨Ь╤Г╨║╨░", "grams": 120}, {"name": "╨Ь╨░╤Б╨╗╨╛", "grams": 210}, {"name": "╨б╨░╤Е╨░╤А", "grams": 180}, {"name": "╨Ц╨╕╤А╨╜╤Л╨╡ ╤Б╨╗╨╕╨▓╨║╨╕", "grams": 15}]	https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/hxcuj01762772827.jpg	2026-05-03 20:15:34.349+00	2026-10-06 13:02:27.379+00	[]	Boil the potatoes. Peel the potatoes while still warm and run them through a potato ricer twice.\r\nтЦв\r\nLet the potatoes cool in an uncovered bowl in the fridge.\r\nтЦв\r\nStir the salt, sugar, melted butter, and cream into the riced potatoes.\r\nтЦв\r\nSlowly add the flour and knead by hand until you get a good consistency. Don't add more flour than necessary! Roll the dough into a long sausage and divide into about 7 or 8 pieces if using an 18 inch griddle. If using a smaller griddle or frying pan, divide the dough into 10 тАУ 12 pieces.\r\nтЦв\r\nRoll each piece into a ball and then press into a flat circle, using the edges of your hands to form the dough into a nice circle shape without any cracks. This is important, otherwise you won't get round lefser.\r\nтЦв\r\nHeat up your griddle on medium/high heat.\r\nтЦв\r\nFlour your rolling surface and roll the lefse dough into a large circle slightly smaller than your griddle or frying pan. Begin rolling with a smooth rolling pin, then switch to a corrugated rolling pin as the lefse gets thinner. Don't use too much flour, as then the edges can become hard.\r\nтЦв\r\nRoll the lefse onto your lefse stick and then gently unroll it onto your griddle. After a minute or two check the underside of the l