0 mins until the sauce thickens slightly. Season to taste. The sauce can be made ahead, then reheated later in the day. Meantime, scrub the mussels or clams and pull away any stringy beards. Any that are open should be tapped sharply on the worktop тАУ if they donтАЩt close after a few seconds, discard them.\r\nReheat the sauce if necessary, then stir the potato, chunks of fish and prawns very gently into the stew. Bring back to the boil, then cover and gently simmer for 3 mins. Scatter the mussels or clams over the stew, then cover and cook for 2 mins more or until the shells have opened wide. Discard any that remain closed. The chunks of fish should flake easily and the prawns should be pink through. Scatter with the thyme leaves.\r\nTo make the quick rouille, stir the rest of the harissa through the mayonnaise. Serve the stew in bowls, topped with spoonfuls of rouille, which will melt into the sauce and enrich it. Have some good bread ready, as youтАЩll definitely want to mop up the juices.	1	\N	France	["╤Г╨╢╨╕╨╜"]	t	https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/532640/summer-fish-stew-with-rouille	mealdb:52918	[{"id": "39eb00c6-1ee3-4f8b-a0e8-63a3aaf12684", "name": "╨Ъ╤А╨╡╨▓╨╡╤В╨║╨╕", "unit": "╨│", "grams": 300, "amount": 300, "ingredientId": "217c513d-310e-4472-adf1-8dc55e9df4bf", "originalString": "300 ╨│"}, {"id": "e090e3e5-1ea6-4774-ace5-3e7b49ceb299", "name": "╨Ю╨╗╨╕╨▓╨║╨╛╨▓╨╛╨╡ ╨╝╨░╤Б╨╗╨╛", "unit": "╨│", "grams": 150, "amount": 150, "ingredientId": "bbc2d001-a24b-49ee-b8ec-16e74e7297ef", "originalString": "150 ╨│"}, {"id": "d324449d-eb20-46a5-a6f5-76d3a916515d", "name": "╨б╤Г╤Е╨╛╨╡ ╨▒╨╡╨╗╨╛╨╡ ╨▓╨╕╨╜╨╛", "unit": "╨│", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "6d84be40-00a1-4bdd-8eda-7103f6aed423", "originalString": "50 ╨│"}, {"id": "eef54f9f-c0cf-462e-88ad-d7a6414d4cd3", "name": "╨а╨╕╨▒╨╜╤Л╨╣ ╨▒╤Г╨╗╤М╨╛╨╜", "unit": "╨│", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "1b880913-4a62-4f19-818f-922cf6e75d73", "originalString": "50 ╨│"}, {"id": "f4fa4b03-b004-4e68-bee6-e1a